{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"400","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Inna and Choose Options"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There always is something to choose from! And now, instead of \"Noughts and Crosses\", Inna choose a very unusual upgrade of this game. The rules of the game are given below:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is one person playing the game. Before the beginning of the game he puts 12 cards in a row on the table. Each card contains a character: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". Then the player chooses two positive integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(a·b = 12)"},{"kind":"text","text":", after that he makes a table of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a × b"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the cards he put on the table as follows: the first "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" cards form the first row of the table, the second "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" cards form the second row of the table and so on, the last "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" cards form the last (number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":") row of the table. The player wins if some column of the table contain characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" on all cards. Otherwise, the player loses."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Inna has already put 12 cards on the table in a row. But unfortunately, she doesn't know what numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" to choose. Help her win the game: print to her all the possible ways of numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a, b"},{"kind":"text","text":" that she can choose and win."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ t ≤ 100)"},{"kind":"text","text":". This value shows the number of sets of test data in the input. Next follows the description of each of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" tests on a separate line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The description of each test is a string consisting of 12 characters, each character is either \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th character of the string shows the character that is written on the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th card from the start."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test, print the answer to the test on a single line. The first number in the line must represent the number of distinct ways to choose the pair "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a, b"},{"kind":"text","text":". Next, print on this line the pairs in the format "},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":"x"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Print the pairs in the order of increasing first parameter ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Separate the pairs in the line by whitespaces."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\nOXXXOXOOXOOX\nOXOXOXOXOXOX\nXXXXXXXXXXXX\nOOOOOOOOOOOO\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 1x12 2x6 4x3\n4 1x12 2x6 3x4 6x2\n6 1x12 2x6 3x4 4x3 6x2 12x1\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"400A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/400/problem/A"}